      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "html": "Format (identical in all four recent exams): <b>15 multiple-choice questions × 3 pt = 45 pt</b> and <b>7 open questions ≈ 64–68 pt</b>, total ≈ 110 pt. Allowed: 4 A4 pages of notes (your formula codex), a non-programmable calculator, the constants table (G, k_B, h, c, m_p, M☉, R☉, pc, Jy, σ_T). Write down intermediate steps."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "html": "The open questions are always: one photometry/angles question, one radiation (blackbody/CMB) question, one stellar-structure or Eddington question, one or two galaxy dynamics questions (virial, rotation curves, tidal, Plummer), one AGN/cluster question, and a Friedmann question at the end."
        },
        {
          "kind": "exam",
          "html": "Mock-exam routine: do one MC set in 30 minutes without hints, then 2-3 open questions (bosses) under their timers. Two official keys contain arithmetic errors (HS24 summer Q2b: 1.77 pW, not 2.5 pW; HS25 practice Q6c: $2.2\\times10^{11}M_\\odot$, not $9.8\\times10^{11}$): trust your own calculation."
        }
      ],
      "check": []
