      "source": {
        "file": "materials/astrophysics/old-exams/Astro_I_2024_Summer_Session_with_Solutions.pdf",
        "where": "HS24 summer: Open Question 5 [9 pt]"
      },
      "instructions": "Derivation: solve on paper, compare with the key points, enter the number.",
      "statement": [
        "A collisionless self-gravitating system of total mass $M$ and $N$ particles of identical mass $m$ is in virial equilibrium.",
        "(a) [3 pt] Show the total kinetic energy is $K=\\frac12M\\sigma_v^2$ with $\\sigma_v^2=\\frac1N\\sum v_i^2$.",
        "(b) [3 pt] Show that for large $N$, $V\\simeq-GM^2/(2r_H)$, where $r_H^{-1}=\\frac{2}{N(N-1)}\\sum_{i>j}r_{ij}^{-1}$.",
        "(c) [3 pt] Show $\\sigma_v^2=GM/(2r_H)$."
      ],
      "finalAnswers": [
        {
          "id": "sig",
          "prompt": "Numbers: $M=10^{12}M_\\odot$, $r_H=100$ kpc. $\\sigma_v$ in km/s.",
          "answer": "sqrt(G*M*Msun/(2*rH*1e3*pc))/1e3",
          "vars": {
